 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Lots of variables at play, like how many coats were done, what kind of oil, and how open or closed is the room. Rough guide is overnight hanging, so several days open. That's still very fresh. Then a light satin is the safe bet, you can get it lookless within few days. A quick wiping varnish like walnut oil comes first, but it only lasts a few hours. It gets really dry within hour or two, you can use it again, it's just that other oils take days or weeks.",
